HOLY CRAP!!!! &nbsp;Thank you! I just figured it out!Reading some of the play-by-play forum posts, as well as the strategy guides... we were only allowing ourselves one &quot;Equipment, Limited&quot; or one &quot;Ongoing, Limited&quot; card per player. Apparently, we misunderstood the rules! You can have many &quot;Whatever, Limited&quot; cards out, but only one of each specific card.So, Wraith could have multiple &quot;Equipment, Limited&quot; cards in play (and actually use two attack powers if one of them is the &quot;Utility Belt&quot;). We were playing that she could only have one &quot;Equipment, Limited&quot; card in play (so I kept having to swap the cards in order to use anything different).UGH!!!!!&nbsp;....oh, and yes, when a hero was incapacitated, we used their incapacitated powers... it&#39;s just that the table basically decided what to do, and the player of that hero was generally left to go eat snacks.&nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Reading your post I wondered if that was what was happening (I&#39;ve been in self-exile to avoid vengeance spoilers so I couldn&#39;t respond sooner). I&#39;ve introduced the game to a few family members and explaining what &quot;limited&quot; meant was always something I had to do at least twice before they got that. Hopefully now you can grudge match Voss and crush under your heel&nbsp; :smiling_imp:
